rkvm-server for Debian
======================

The package deliberately does not enable or start rkvm-server on first install.
The server grabs physical input devices, so an incorrect configuration can leave
the local display without usable keyboard or mouse input.

Initial setup:

  sudo install -d -m 0700 /etc/rkvm
  sudo cp /usr/share/doc/rkvm-server/examples/server.toml /etc/rkvm/server.toml
  sudo rkvm-certificate-gen /etc/rkvm/certificate.pem /etc/rkvm/key.pem \
      --ip-addresses 192.0.2.10 --days 3650
  sudo chmod 0600 /etc/rkvm/server.toml /etc/rkvm/key.pem

Replace 192.0.2.10 with the server address used by clients and replace the
example password in server.toml with a long random value. Test the configuration
before enabling the service:

  sudo rkvm-server /etc/rkvm/server.toml --shutdown-after 15
  sudo systemctl enable --now rkvm-server.service

The example uses left Alt plus left Ctrl to switch destinations. Package removal
does not delete /etc/rkvm, its private key, certificate, or configuration.
